  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Isoelectric series:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />All have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> electrons. In the isoelectronic series, the&nbsp;proton/electron ratio decreases, so the size decrease because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></math> increases on decrease proton/electron ratio.</p>"
